[[:db/retract 17592186157803 :question/answer-fields 17592186155739] [:db/retract 17592186157632 :question/answer-fields 17592186154040] [:db/retract 17592186157632 :question/answer-fields 17592186154034] [:db/retract 17592186157632 :question/answer-fields 17592186154043] [:db/retract 17592186157632 :question/answer-fields 17592186154037] {:db/id 17592186157231 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b8076c0f-174e-5d1d-bedf-553b0bcc1d94"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157803 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are logically equivalent?\n\n- $X∧¬Y$\n- $¬(Y∨¬X)$\n- $¬Y∧(X∨X)$" :question/worked-solution "Two statements are logically equivalent if they have the same truth table. So, we construct a truth table for the three given statements:\n\n| $\\,X\\,$ | $\\,Y\\,$ | $\\,X∧¬Y\\,$ | $\\,¬(Y∨¬X)\\,$ | $\\,¬Y∧(X∨X)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nWe see that all three statements have the same truth table, so they are logically equivalent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a8dd17e7-0d8b-5c3d-969d-d2b55a8096cf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a8dd17e7-0d8b-5c3d-969d-d2b55a8096cf" :answer-field/id #uuid "a8dd17e7-0d8b-5c3d-969d-d2b55a8096cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c8d4fe98-d76d-5dbf-a213-a80be0e92e5f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cd49cdaa-1cf5-560d-8136-100f799a29cf" "answer-749528c1-877b-55f6-b18e-8021de390991" "answer-c8d4fe98-d76d-5dbf-a213-a80be0e92e5f" "answer-7a382814-419c-5c02-b340-0b80ee5d5e86" "answer-4d46c836-fa