717-d982-51ef-bc12-71e8f554d51e" :answer/id #uuid "42f09717-d982-51ef-bc12-71e8f554d51e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-31ca1a18-e271-54de-8d6a-f0aa14857b82" :question/id #uuid "31ca1a18-e271-54de-8d6a-f0aa14857b82" :question/math-academy-id "q-182517" :question/problem "Find the missing values in the following truth table:" :question/worked-solution "First, let's solve for the missing values:\n\n- When $A≡\\text{T}$ and $B≡\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B) & ≡(\\text{T}∧\\text{T})∨¬(\\text{T}∨¬\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡(\\text{T}∧\\text{T})∨¬(\\text{T}∨\\text{F}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∨¬\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $A≡\\text{T}$ and $B≡\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B) & ≡(\\text{T}∧\\text{F})∨¬(\\text{T}∨¬\\text{F}) \\\\  & ≡(\\text{T}∧\\text{F})∨¬(\\text{T}∨\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∨¬\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∨\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $A≡\\text{F}$ and $B≡\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B) & ≡(\\text{F}∧\\text{T})∨¬(\\text{F}∨¬\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∨¬\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∨\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur completed table is shown below.\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nTo determine whether $(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B)$ is logically equivalent to $A,$ we need to check whether their truth tables are equivalent.\n\nWe see that the columns for $(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B)$ and $A$ are different. They differ in the second and third rows. Therefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B)≢A.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-35f1d21e-f525-5bb3-81dc-dc1d4446e2c7" "answer-field-d440bf3f-9095-526